<title>GERMANY: D.Telekom, Mannesmann form venture.</title>
<headline>D.Telekom, Mannesmann form venture.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>German telecommunications groups Deutsche Telekom AG and Mannesmann AG said on Monday they have formed a venture to gather traffic information.</p>
<p>Called DDG, the venture would begin operations immediately gathering information on traffic jams, emergency services, routing and navigation on major German roadways. Mannesmann's Eurokom unit and Telkom MobilNet each own 50 percent of DDG.</p>
<p>The venture would invest in systems and equipment to expand coverage in Germany, but would confine it activities to data gathering. Mannesmann Autocom and Telekom's T-Traffic businesses would compete in distributing the information to motorists or other potential customers.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
